{"book":56,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"Teaching That Adorns the Gospel","summary":"Paul gives Titus instructions for older men and women, younger women and men, and slaves, grounding them in God's grace, which teaches godly living while believers await Christ's appearing.","background":"Outsiders watched how the new faith affected households, and Christians were sometimes accused of disrupting family order. Paul repeatedly gives the reason for his instructions: so 'that the word of God be not blasphemed' (v. 5) and so believers 'may adorn the doctrine of God' (v. 10). Older women are to train younger ones, a role Titus himself does not take.","customs":[{"term":"Adorn","verses":"2:10","note":"The Greek word, related to English 'cosmetic', means to arrange or decorate so as to make attractive."},{"term":"Purloining","verses":"2:10","note":"Slaves often handled their masters' goods and money; pilfering small amounts was a common temptation and complaint."}],"watchFor":["Grace is described as a teacher (vv. 11–12).","'That blessed hope' of Christ's appearing (v. 13)."],"connections":["Ezekiel 37:23","Deuteronomy 14:2","Exodus 19:5","1 Peter 2:9"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Σὺ","Su","G4771","P-2NS","You yourself"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","however"],["λάλει","lalei","G2980","V-PAM-2S","do speak"],["ἃ","ha","G3739","R-NPN","[the things] that"],["πρέπει","prepei","G4241","V-PAI-3S","are consistent with"],["τῇ","tēa","G3588","T-DSF","<the>"],["ὑγιαινούσῃ","hugiainousē","G5198","V-PAP-DSF","sound"],["διδασκαλίᾳ","didaskalia","G1319","N-DSF","doctrine"]],"x":[[55001013,55001013,13],[54006003,54006003,9],[56001009,56001009,6],[54001010,54001010,5],[56003008,56003008,5],[56002011,56002014,4]],"xn":6},"2":{"w":[["Πρεσβύτας","Presbutas","G4246","N-APM","[The] aged [men]"],["νηφαλίους","nēphalious","G3524","A-APM","sober-minded"],["εἶναι","einai","G1511","V-PAN","are to be"],["σεμνούς","semnous","G4586","A-APM","dignified"],["σώφρονας","sōphronas","G4998","A-APM","s